<!-- INTRODUCTION SECTION -->
<section class="acdt-intro content-section" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <h2 id="intro-heading" class="sr-only">About GMT to CST Conversion</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to our official <strong>GMT to CST Converter</strong>. Coordinating communication between London and the heartland of North American commerce in Chicago, Dallas, and Houston requires managing a <strong>6-hour time difference</strong>. Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) operates as the universal zero baseline at Coordinated Universal Time +0 (UTC+0), whereas Central Standard Time (CST) operates at UTC-6. As a result, Central Standard Time is exactly 6 hours behind Greenwich Mean Time.
  </p>
  <p>
    The 6-hour offset creates a productive 3-to-4 hour overlap window during standard business days. When professionals in London or Dublin return from lunch at 3:00 PM GMT, business teams across Chicago, Dallas, Minneapolis, and Mexico City are starting their workday at 9:00 AM CST.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our online utility calculates precise conversion results using native browser localization APIs backed by official IANA database keys (`UTC` and `America/Chicago`). Whether you manage energy trading desks in Houston, futures trading at CME Group in Chicago, or corporate logistics across Texas and the Midwest, this guide provides real-time dual clocks, interactive 24-hour schedules, meeting planners, and detailed regional context.
  </p>
</section>

