        Converting GMT hours between 12:00 AM and 5:59 AM shifts the CST time back into the previous calendar evening.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>2. Confusing CST (US) with CST (China)</h3>
      <p>
        China Standard Time (UTC+8) shares the CST acronym but is 14 hours ahead of US Central Standard Time (UTC-6). Ensure your system targets North American Central Time.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>3. Overlooking Spring/Fall DST Shift Weeks</h3>
      <p>
        Assuming the gap is strictly 6 hours during March and October transition weeks will lead to 1-hour scheduling mismatches.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
